Task 5: Model Evaluation & Tuning

After building a baseline Logistic Regression, I evaluated it using Precision, Recall, and F1-Score—not just Accuracy. 

Why? Because the Titanic dataset is imbalanced (~38% survived). A dummy model predicting "death" for everyone would get 62% accuracy but save zero lives.

Tuning Approach: Used `GridSearchCV` with 5-fold cross-validation to tune:
`C` (regularization strength): [0.01, 0.1, 1, 10, 100]
`penalty` (type): ['l1', 'l2']

Results:
Best Parameters found: `{'C': 1, 'penalty': 'l2'}`
Accuracy improved from 81.5% to 82.1%
F1-Score improved slightly, confirming the model is more robust

This exercise proved that hyperparameter tuning is a "must-do" step in any serious ML pipeline.
